{
  "_readme": [
    "Example override for {config_dir}/labels.json -- ibcontroller init/run copy this",
    "file as labels.json.example, NOT as labels.json: labels.load_labels() applies",
    "{config_dir}/labels.json unconditionally the moment it exists, so activating an",
    "override is a deliberate rename, never automatic.",
    "",
    "labels.py's own _deep_merge overrides one field at a time -- you only need to name",
    "the label that actually changed, not repeat every sibling field or every other",
    "domain untouched. This file is trimmed down to two illustrative examples, not a",
    "full copy of the bundled data/labels.json:",
    "",
    "  - login.gateway_titles: shows how to add a title variant IBKR renamed/localized",
    "    (the override REPLACES the whole list, so include every title you still want,",
    "    not just the new one).",
    "  - dismiss_rules: this one is a list, not a nested object, so an override replaces",
    "    the whole list rather than merging entry by entry -- copy the bundled entries",
    "    here (as done below) before adding your own, or you'll lose the built-in ones.",
    "",
    "Remove this _readme key before using the file for real -- it is not a real Labels",
    "field and is harmless where cattrs ignores unknown keys, but it's not meant to ship.",
    "See labels.py's own module docstring and DismissRule's docstring for the full",
    "mechanism."
  ],
  "login": {
    "gateway_titles": [
      "IBKR Gateway",
      "IB Gateway",
      "Interactive Brokers Gateway"
    ]
  },
  "dismiss_rules": [
    {
      "name": "non_brokerage_account",
      "match_text": "This is not a brokerage account",
      "click": "I understand and accept"
    },
    {
      "name": "auto_restart_confirmation",
      "match_text": "trading platform restart automatically",
      "click": "OK"
    }
  ]
}
